 "anomalies": [
  "Rust talker does not disable core dumps (C calls prctl(PR_SET_DUMPABLE,0)): each --crash-after abort was \"core dumped\" via systemd-coredump (5 dumps in coredumpctl); restart cycle ~2.26 s vs C 2.20 s, so Rust saw 5 aborts in the 15 s window vs 6 for C.",
  "Rust talker has no SIGTERM handler: under the manager it is \"killed by signal 15\" and standalone exits 143 without close(), leaving flags=0 (C talker exits 0 and sets flags bit 0 closed).",
  "C writes writer_pid at header offset 152 (as docs/01-topics.md defines); Rust leaves it 0 (SPEC.md lists no field there). Did not affect interop.",
  "C listener reports gaps=1 in one of three 20 s latency runs (no torn, max 217 us); likely the ring backlog it reads at attach (starts at W-K+2) being overwritten before it is read; Rust starts at the next message and showed 0 gaps.",
  "msgs differ by design: C listener counts the ~15 backlog messages at attach (20016) vs Rust 20001.",
  "Registry in backoff: C writes pid/starttime 0 0; Rust keeps the dead pid and starttime. Running with 0 failures: C delay_s 0, Rust 0.1.",
  "Rust RSS ~3-4x C (manager idle 480 vs 136 kB; talker ~380 vs ~122 kB; listener ~484-548 vs 204 kB); binaries ~8x larger.",
  "Both idle managers: 0 voluntary/nonvoluntary context switches and 0 CPU ticks over 30 s.",
  "One C clean-build timing outlier (1.27 s, others 0.21-0.57 s), probably desktop load."
 ]
